WEBVTT

00:11:57.242 --> 00:12:00.253
Basically, structured
interviews get you better data,

00:12:00.277 --> 00:12:04.033
and that strategy can help solve
some of our misjudgments in hiring,

00:12:04.057 --> 00:12:05.808
but not all of them.

00:12:05.832 --> 00:12:08.482
There's a third problem
with the traditional interview.

00:12:08.506 --> 00:12:10.317
No matter how good your questions are,

00:12:10.341 --> 00:12:12.738
you still pick up more noise than signal,

00:12:12.762 --> 00:12:14.603
and one of the most distracting noises

00:12:14.627 --> 00:12:16.628
is interviewer biases.

00:12:16.652 --> 00:12:19.904
LR: Interviewers make up their minds
about who they're going to hire,

00:12:19.928 --> 00:12:22.069
if they like this candidate
in front of them,

00:12:22.093 --> 00:12:23.416
within the first, you know,

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.337
usually the data says under 90 seconds.

00:12:25.361 --> 00:12:28.035
And if you think of what happens
in the first 90 seconds,

00:12:28.059 --> 00:12:29.210
say, of a job interview,

00:12:29.234 --> 00:12:31.245
it's things like, physical attractiveness,